        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "eb57df2e-a6e3-5031-8119-44bb995d63f3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Publications: Ainslee's Magazine, The Australian Women's Weekly, Strand Magazine, Woman's Day, New Idea\n- People: Nene King\n- Works: The Prince and Betty\n- Companies: Bauer Media Group\n- Places: United States, United Kingdom, Sydney, Australia\n\nFacts:\n- Ainslee's Magazine was an American literary periodical published from 1897 to December 1926.\n- The Prince and Betty was originally published in Ainslee's Magazine in the United States in January 1912.\n- The Prince and Betty was published in a slightly different form as a serial in Strand Magazine in the United Kingdom between February and April 1912.\n- The Australian Women's Weekly is an Australian monthly women's magazine published by Bauer Media Group in Sydney.\n- Nene King was the former editor of Woman's Day, New Idea, and The Australian Women's Weekly.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "415d4dec-9066-5a21-85d2-d3a9fa1e5009",
        "text": "Page: Ainslee's Magazine. Sentence: Ainslee's Magazine was an American literary periodical published from 1897 to December 1926.\nPage: The Australian Women's Weekly. Sentence: The Australian Women's Weekly, sometimes known as simply \"The Weekly\", is an Australian monthly women's magazine published by Bauer Media Group in Sydney.\nPage: The Prince and Betty. Sentence: It was originally published in \"Ainslee's Magazine\" in the United States in January 1912, and, in a slightly different form, as a serial in \"Strand Magazine\" in the United Kingdom between February and April 1912.\nPage: Nene King. Sentence: She is the former editor of some of Australia's most famous women's magazines, including \"Woman's Day\", \"New Idea\" and \"Women's Weekly\".",
